{"nodes": [{"id": "supabase_tests_opening_close_test_opening_close_test", "label": "opening_close_test (card ^ref-62)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "supabase/tests/opening_close_test.sql", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Failure-case suite for fn_close_opening_balances and fn_backdating_allowed, TC-25 ... TC-37 and TC-40 of TDD-opening-balance.md. Its own file because the close is permanent WITHIN a transaction too, so each case runs inside a plpgsql sub-block and leaves by raising ROLLBACK_TO_OPEN, using the implicit savepoint around a BEGIN ... EXCEPTION block to unwind the close; anything that is not the sentinel is re-raised so an assert still fails the file. Asserts: the close must not succeed over a costless row, which could then never be costed and never re-entered (Seam 1); a retry must not read as a second close of the one operation the Owner cannot undo (R4 against TC-29); an OPENING row must be refused after the close even through fn_post_ledger (Seam 2); R28 must not re-arm by a second mechanism that can disagree with the first (Seam 4); the back-dating boundary must be the same on every screen (R28); unlock_max_days_back must be configured, not assumed as 3 (ADR-023, BR23)."}], "edges": [{"source": "supabase_tests_opening_close_test_opening_close_test", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_close_opening_balances_fn_close_opening_balances", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/opening_close_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_tests_opening_close_test_opening_close_test", "target": "supabase_functions_fn_backdating_allowed_fn_backdating_allowed", "relation": "calls", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "supabase/tests/opening_close_test.sql", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "supabase_tests_opening_close_test_opening